WEBVTT

01:46.170 --> 01:48.250
I'm Hono Akira, attorney-at-law.

01:49.050 --> 01:51.040
Don't worry.

01:51.040 --> 01:55.710
Now that I've taken this case, we will win.

01:55.710 --> 01:57.590
That was amazing, Jinguji-kun.

01:57.590 --> 02:01.330
You have an impressive grasp
of Hono Akira's character.

02:01.330 --> 02:04.310
I still have a lot to improve upon.

02:04.310 --> 02:07.670
Boy! That was amazing!

02:07.670 --> 02:11.380
That's STARISH for you!

02:11.380 --> 02:13.190
You guys have some real energy!

02:13.190 --> 02:16.830
Hey, Kiryuin-kun. Don't just
sit there acting impressed.

02:17.730 --> 02:18.930
You're right.

02:18.930 --> 02:21.050
Kiryuin-kun, you give it a try.

02:21.050 --> 02:23.300
Sure. Let's see...

02:23.770 --> 02:26.450
I'm Kazeno Sosuke, attorney-at-law.

02:27.290 --> 02:30.540
When I take a case, I don't lose.

02:30.540 --> 02:34.970
Guys who try to sue big businesses
are just in it for the money.

02:35.960 --> 02:37.630
Your energy's kind of low.

02:37.630 --> 02:40.800
Oh, sorry. But today's my
first time reading the script.

02:41.290 --> 02:43.550
Van-kun is a slow starter.

02:43.550 --> 02:47.050
Yeah, so go easy on me.

02:48.280 --> 02:50.020
Kiryuin Van.

02:50.760 --> 02:52.910
He's different from what I expected.

02:54.480 --> 02:56.550
I can't believe you're costarring

02:56.550 --> 02:59.150
in a two-hour TV special
with your duet project partner.

02:59.150 --> 03:01.360
Doesn't it feel like it's meant to be?

03:01.360 --> 03:03.950
Yeah, I guess.

03:04.650 --> 03:07.430
You met him yesterday
at the read-through, right?

03:07.430 --> 03:09.090
What is he like?

03:09.090 --> 03:10.470
What is he like?

03:10.930 --> 03:15.540
I wouldn't want to give you
any preconceived ideas about him.

03:15.540 --> 03:20.260
Oh, you're right. The script
for the show was interesting.

03:20.260 --> 03:26.060
Monday Drama

03:20.260 --> 03:26.060
Wind and Fire

03:21.180 --> 03:26.060
You're playing lawyers
with a long-standing rivalry.

03:26.060 --> 03:26.510
Hey!

03:27.430 --> 03:29.140
Jinguji Ren-chan.

03:29.140 --> 03:31.000
Good work yesterday.

03:31.000 --> 03:32.770
I look forward to working with you!

03:33.950 --> 03:35.590
So do I.

03:35.590 --> 03:36.900
Huh? What?

03:38.440 --> 03:39.600
Ha-chan.

03:40.490 --> 03:41.400
Ha-chan?

03:41.400 --> 03:45.330
We finally meet again. I'm so happy.

03:45.330 --> 03:47.620
I'm expecting a great song from you.

03:47.620 --> 03:49.370
Uh... Okay.

03:50.560 --> 03:54.750
My little lamb always writes great songs.

03:56.090 --> 03:58.440
Really? I see.

03:59.770 --> 04:03.970
In the TV show, his character's
concept is wind, and mine is fire.

04:04.530 --> 04:07.610
Why don't we incorporate that
into the duet project?

04:08.090 --> 04:13.270
We can start with two contrasting
melodies that gradually come together.

04:13.270 --> 04:15.310
Sounds like what everyone would expect.

04:16.090 --> 04:17.230
What everyone would expect

04:17.230 --> 04:20.980
Instead, let's have a real adventure
with some big surprises!

04:20.980 --> 04:26.120
Let's give it to them good from the start
and raise the intensity from there.

04:26.120 --> 04:28.690
What does that mean?
Could you be more specific?

04:28.690 --> 04:32.580
You mean start with an impactful hook,

04:32.580 --> 04:37.710
bring in the strings,
and layer on surprising phrases?

04:37.710 --> 04:39.550
Yeah, exactly.

04:40.790 --> 04:43.260
You've got it. I'm glad.

04:43.260 --> 04:45.010
I'm so glad.

04:45.010 --> 04:46.220
I knew you'd get it, Ha-chan.

04:50.610 --> 04:53.800
Scary, scary. Ren-chan, don't be such a downer.

04:53.800 --> 04:55.640
You're not as much fun as I thought.

04:56.010 --> 04:57.390
Just kidding.

04:59.190 --> 05:03.110
We didn't end up making
any concrete decisions.

05:03.110 --> 05:07.630
Next time, we should suggest
some practical concepts.

05:07.630 --> 05:08.410
You're right.

05:10.350 --> 05:13.120
I'm sorry. I left my papers there.

05:22.730 --> 05:24.090
E-Excuse me.

05:24.750 --> 05:25.880
Ha-chan.

05:27.600 --> 05:31.630
It must be fate that
brought us together again.

05:31.630 --> 05:32.220
What?

05:32.720 --> 05:35.480
We mustn't defy the god of destiny.

05:35.480 --> 05:37.140
We should start dating.

05:37.140 --> 05:39.430
What? U-Um...

05:39.430 --> 05:41.910
We know we get along really well.

05:41.910 --> 05:44.320
Don't you want to know more about me?

05:44.320 --> 05:46.360
I promise you'll fall in love with me.

05:49.580 --> 05:50.950
Jinguji-san.

05:52.760 --> 05:53.770
What do you want?

05:54.480 --> 05:56.290
I'm not interested in pranks.

05:56.290 --> 05:57.500
Pranks?

05:57.500 --> 06:00.880
I'm not joking. I'm always serious.

06:02.470 --> 06:04.840
My lady, you go on ahead.

06:04.840 --> 06:05.760
Um...

06:06.600 --> 06:07.800
Go.

06:11.170 --> 06:12.700
She's our composer.

06:13.310 --> 06:16.810
What do you think you're doing when
we're about to start working with her?

06:18.330 --> 06:21.110
So you do like her, Ren-chan.

06:22.190 --> 06:28.080
I really like her, so I told her how I felt.

06:28.080 --> 06:32.950
I'm honest about my feelings, unlike you.

06:32.950 --> 06:35.460
You don't know anything about me.

06:35.460 --> 06:38.160
I'm true to myself.

06:38.160 --> 06:41.510
Every day is an adventure. Life is for keeps.

06:41.510 --> 06:44.310
And I believe that's connected to music, too.

06:44.970 --> 06:49.340
If you lie to yourself, your music is a lie, too.

06:50.490 --> 06:52.720
The people listening can tell.

06:54.480 --> 06:57.100
I'm not lying to myself.

07:00.770 --> 07:03.650
In any case, Ren-chan,
you should give a little more effort.

07:03.650 --> 07:04.940
I don't need to hear that from you.

07:05.910 --> 07:08.020
Let's have a contest.

07:08.660 --> 07:09.650
A contest?

07:10.790 --> 07:14.580
Whoever receives higher praise for their
performance in the TV show gets Ha-chan.

07:14.580 --> 07:17.120
What? She's not a thing!

07:17.120 --> 07:18.650
Boy! You're scary.

07:19.930 --> 07:21.850
I'm getting out of here.

07:22.750 --> 07:24.820
Don't run from our contest.

07:31.350 --> 07:36.000
I haven't felt this much anger
towards someone in a long time.

07:37.970 --> 07:39.030
Um...

07:39.690 --> 07:43.580
Oh. Sorry, little lamb. It's all right.

07:43.580 --> 07:48.130
I'll do all I need to do
for the show and the duet project.

07:49.280 --> 07:50.230
With everything I've got.

07:52.730 --> 07:55.340
Eiichi, I understand how you feel now.

07:56.350 --> 08:00.160
You've always said you wanted
Nanami Haruka to be ours.

08:00.160 --> 08:03.120
Yeah. She's good.

08:04.760 --> 08:06.330
She will be mine.

08:09.460 --> 08:12.410
We haven't done a job together in a while.

08:12.410 --> 08:14.960
How is the duet project coming along?

08:14.960 --> 08:18.560
Kiryuin-san is the oldest
member of HEAVENS, isn't he?

08:18.560 --> 08:22.310
Kiryuin Van. Honestly, I'm disappointed...

08:22.730 --> 08:25.630
What he says and what
he does are totally different.

08:25.630 --> 08:27.330
Really?

08:27.330 --> 08:31.410
His acting for the show
is still totally unempathetic.

08:31.410 --> 08:33.400
Doesn't filming start soon?

08:33.400 --> 08:35.050
That can't be good.

08:35.600 --> 08:37.910
That's weird, though.

08:38.620 --> 08:42.960
I heard he was really good
as a guest star in another show.

08:42.960 --> 08:43.800
What?

08:49.410 --> 08:54.050
His acting is good? That's just a rumor.

08:54.050 --> 08:58.640
Besides, why is he so relaxed
when we're about to start shooting?

09:00.480 --> 09:02.130
He doesn't stand a chance.

09:03.230 --> 09:05.190
We're ready to start shooting.

09:05.600 --> 09:07.870
Scene 12, take one.

09:07.870 --> 09:09.110
Ready...

09:13.360 --> 09:14.400
Start!

09:16.130 --> 09:18.410
I'm Kazeno Sosuke, attorney-at-law.

09:18.410 --> 09:19.450
What?

09:19.450 --> 09:23.300
There it is. This is the real Kiryuin Van.

09:23.300 --> 09:25.210
I-I see.

09:25.210 --> 09:29.590
When I take a case, I don't lose.

09:30.460 --> 09:32.670
That's my line.

09:34.630 --> 09:37.920
I'll put everything on the line
and fight for the plaintiff.

09:45.770 --> 09:47.310
Cut!

09:48.730 --> 09:55.860
Ren-kun, the breathlessness you showed after
Van-kun said his lines was really good.

09:57.850 --> 09:58.810
Thank you.

10:01.970 --> 10:03.210
That wasn't acting.

10:04.010 --> 10:08.540
I really was left breathless after
being overwhelmed by his acting.

10:08.540 --> 10:11.740
Anyway, it sure is hot today.

10:11.740 --> 10:14.480
Make sure you stay hydrated.

10:14.480 --> 10:15.990
Okay.

10:15.990 --> 10:17.800
He was like another person.

10:18.830 --> 10:21.890
Was that his true strength?

10:22.590 --> 10:26.560
He lets it build up and
releases it when it's time.

10:28.160 --> 10:31.410
I had no idea. I underestimated him.

10:32.020 --> 10:35.070
I can't forgive myself for that.

10:41.480 --> 10:42.630
Jinguji.

10:46.480 --> 10:48.200
How unusual, Jinguji.

10:49.860 --> 10:51.710
What is it, Hijirikawa?

10:51.710 --> 10:57.380
You do everything so flawlessly,
I've never seen you look so desperate before.

10:57.380 --> 11:00.100
What? I see.

11:02.970 --> 11:06.140
I guess he lit a fire under me.

11:06.140 --> 11:09.350
A fire? You mean Kiryuin Van?

11:09.350 --> 11:10.140
Yeah.

11:11.210 --> 11:17.030
Right now, I want to do whatever
it takes to beat him.

11:17.490 --> 11:19.030
Jinguji.

11:20.390 --> 11:23.050
I will beat him at this contest.

11:23.610 --> 11:26.630
For my lady and for STARISH.

11:27.330 --> 11:30.040
And for myself.

11:36.180 --> 11:38.000
Jinguji Ren.

11:40.490 --> 11:43.430
I haven't had to try this hard in a while.

11:44.320 --> 11:47.220
Every day is an adventure. Life is for keeps.

11:48.060 --> 11:50.790
Interesting. This is starting
to get interesting.

12:30.020 --> 12:33.060
We're finally shooting
the climactic courtroom scene.

12:33.380 --> 12:37.520
On one side is the father of a child
injured by a defective product.

12:37.520 --> 12:41.820
On the other is the large corporation
insisting it wasn't their fault.

12:42.420 --> 12:45.530
The plaintiff and father's lawyer is Ren-kun.

12:45.530 --> 12:48.990
And the corporation's lawyer is Van-kun.

12:51.710 --> 12:56.840
The two of you will make sparks fly
in the show's biggest scene.

13:06.010 --> 13:08.300
The set is incredible.

13:08.300 --> 13:11.220
It's like a real courtroom.

13:13.120 --> 13:14.300
Jinguji-san.

13:18.420 --> 13:23.290
My lady, I want you to see me
act with everything on the line.

13:28.030 --> 13:32.200
Ha-chan, watch me as I act my heart out.

13:37.660 --> 13:40.000
Ready, start!

13:40.000 --> 13:43.170
In other words, it's a
question of compensation.

13:43.170 --> 13:44.810
No, I...

13:45.800 --> 13:48.930
By the way, you happen to be in debt.

13:49.810 --> 13:52.350
If you were paid damages,
you could pay off—

13:52.350 --> 13:55.810
Objection! That question
has nothing to do with this case.

13:55.810 --> 13:57.640
Objection sustained.

14:02.390 --> 14:04.320
There's so much tension.

14:04.320 --> 14:05.190
Yeah.

14:05.190 --> 14:09.980
This product is the culmination of Ingenics'
techniques and the pride of the company.

14:09.980 --> 14:13.310
User satisfaction is over 97 percent.

14:13.310 --> 14:19.370
But a child has been injured, even though
he was using it according to the manual.

14:19.370 --> 14:22.340
There's no proof he was following the manual.

14:23.050 --> 14:28.010
Even you must understand
a number as large as 97 percent.

14:28.010 --> 14:29.320
Who cares about numbers?

14:29.320 --> 14:33.370
If you're engaged in manufacturing,
you should see the faces of your consumers.

14:33.370 --> 14:34.930
What? You're not making any sense.

14:34.930 --> 14:38.640
I'm saying you should put yourself
in their shoes and really think about it.

14:43.860 --> 14:46.820
The motto of Ingenics' founder is...

14:46.820 --> 14:50.050
"Every day is an adventure!
Life is for keeps!"

14:50.760 --> 14:52.490
That wasn't in the script.

14:52.490 --> 14:54.790
In order to seize the hearts of their users,

14:54.790 --> 14:57.200
they make products
with all they've got

14:57.200 --> 14:58.460
while remaining true to themselves.

14:58.460 --> 15:00.500
There it is. Van-kun's ad-libbing.

15:00.500 --> 15:01.390
Sir?

15:01.390 --> 15:03.520
It's fine. Keep rolling.

15:03.520 --> 15:06.420
If we stop now, we'll lose this intense heat.

15:07.600 --> 15:09.630
What will you do now, Jinguji?

15:10.150 --> 15:13.680
Can you accept my challenge?

15:17.430 --> 15:20.270
Everything they have, huh?

15:20.270 --> 15:21.950
That's it. Come on.

15:22.520 --> 15:27.190
It's true that Ingenics has developed
a lot of impressive products.

15:27.870 --> 15:29.850
Ren-kun is responding to his ad-libbing.

15:29.850 --> 15:30.820
Good.

15:31.760 --> 15:33.490
Jinguji-san.

15:33.490 --> 15:40.410
That's right. Products made honestly
and earnestly will make the user happy.

15:40.410 --> 15:43.330
Ingenics is confident they can do that.

15:43.330 --> 15:48.130
Are you sure that confidence
hasn't turned to arrogance?

15:49.580 --> 15:50.630
Arrogance?

15:50.630 --> 15:55.420
That's right. You arrogantly assume
you can make them happy no matter what.

15:55.840 --> 15:57.890
Or perhaps you only care about your own needs!

15:57.890 --> 16:03.020
I only care about myself? You're just saying that because you can't play for keeps!

16:03.020 --> 16:06.000
Even if you're "playing for keeps", if you don't consider the feelings of others,

16:06.000 --> 16:07.970
you're simply imposing your own feelings on them.

16:09.120 --> 16:14.800
What do they most need now,
and what can I do about it?

16:15.530 --> 16:21.330
Always putting myself in the shoes
of others is what I'm all about!

16:31.230 --> 16:32.130
Your Honor.

16:33.860 --> 16:34.510
Yes?

16:34.980 --> 16:37.260
I'd like to submit the next piece of evidence.

16:37.670 --> 16:39.600
I-I'll allow it.

16:39.600 --> 16:40.470
All right.

16:40.470 --> 16:42.710
Cut!

16:52.410 --> 16:54.790
That ad-lib came out of nowhere.

16:54.790 --> 16:56.620
I'm impressed you were able to keep up.

16:56.620 --> 16:59.030
Interesting, wasn't it?

16:59.030 --> 17:01.910
Yeah, it was really interesting.

17:01.910 --> 17:04.900
I'll admit we were evenly matched.

17:04.900 --> 17:06.290
There are no winners or losers here.

17:06.290 --> 17:08.520
Yeah, you're right.

17:09.130 --> 17:12.020
Ren-kun, that was great.

17:12.020 --> 17:13.420
Thank you.

17:13.420 --> 17:16.600
You gave an impressive response
to Van-kun's ad-libbing.

17:16.930 --> 17:18.380
The director spoke very highly of you, too.

17:18.380 --> 17:21.000
That scene we just shot was on fire.

17:22.060 --> 17:25.080
We're thinking about turning
this special into a series.

17:25.080 --> 17:27.180
I look forward to working with you again.

17:27.180 --> 17:27.920
Sure.

17:28.490 --> 17:29.610
See you later.

17:36.420 --> 17:37.280
My lady?

17:41.130 --> 17:43.910
Um... What did you want to tell me?

17:44.370 --> 17:45.760
I'm in love with you.

17:45.760 --> 17:47.350
Will you go out with me?

17:47.350 --> 17:48.310
Huh?

17:48.310 --> 17:53.630
I'm serious. If you choose me,
I promise you'll be happy.

17:53.630 --> 17:54.590
I swear it.

17:55.420 --> 17:57.630
Tell me how you really feel.

18:06.060 --> 18:08.230
U-Um...

18:10.860 --> 18:15.050
All I can think about right now is music.

18:20.140 --> 18:20.910
Huh?

18:22.800 --> 18:25.410
You really are an interesting girl, Ha-chan.

18:25.410 --> 18:26.330
What?

18:32.750 --> 18:35.290
I hope you'll write a really great song for us.

18:35.850 --> 18:38.630
I'll do an awesome job singing it.

18:39.620 --> 18:40.430
Okay.

18:40.970 --> 18:45.350
Thanks for listening.
See you at the next meeting.

18:45.350 --> 18:46.960
Okay. See you later.

18:51.180 --> 18:54.070
I won't give up, though.

18:54.400 --> 18:59.900
The first time I heard "HEAVENSGATE,"
I fell in love with you.

19:00.320 --> 19:02.970
I can't give up that easily.

19:10.800 --> 19:15.800
My heart is a wind that's
always blowing towards you.

19:23.550 --> 19:24.300
Where is she?

19:24.300 --> 19:28.090
You just missed her.
She headed back to the studio.

19:28.090 --> 19:29.510
What do you think you're doing?

19:29.510 --> 19:31.100
You said we were evenly matched.

19:31.100 --> 19:33.270
Don't worry. She rejected me.

19:34.080 --> 19:35.260
I see.

19:35.260 --> 19:39.370
If you're so serious about her,
why don't you tell her how you feel?

19:42.300 --> 19:44.150
It's because I'm serious about her.

19:45.770 --> 19:47.900
She's important to me.

19:48.570 --> 19:51.530
I used to think I would
never belong to anyone.

19:51.530 --> 19:53.480
I thought I was a preacher of love.

19:54.100 --> 19:56.880
But my heart was always empty.

19:58.050 --> 20:01.590
She opened the door to music for me.

20:01.930 --> 20:05.220
She showed me the way with her warm light.

20:06.720 --> 20:12.350
That's why I put her happiness before mine.

20:14.150 --> 20:19.730
Right now, she should be working towards
the Triple S decisive concert.

20:20.170 --> 20:23.620
She loves music more than anything else.

20:23.620 --> 20:27.450
That's why I want to watch over her right now.

20:27.450 --> 20:31.830
That's how I truly love a person.

20:33.380 --> 20:36.460
I admit it. I lost.

20:37.380 --> 20:39.920
But only for now.

20:40.330 --> 20:45.300
If your conviction wavers even a little,
you'd better prepare yourself.

20:46.310 --> 20:47.810
I see.

20:47.810 --> 20:50.830
But there won't be any need for that.

20:55.380 --> 20:56.900
You're the greatest.

20:56.900 --> 20:59.970
I really want to sing a duet with you now.

20:59.970 --> 21:02.970
Together, we could sing our hearts out.

21:02.970 --> 21:04.820
Yeah, you're right.

21:18.580 --> 21:23.210
Let's go, my dear, the rendezvous
is starting again tonight

21:23.210 --> 21:28.240
Give me your hand, my dear,
which will you choose

21:28.240 --> 21:28.720
Burn out

21:28.720 --> 21:30.390
With seething flames

21:30.390 --> 21:31.060
Rush out

21:31.060 --> 21:32.770
And dancing wind

21:32.770 --> 21:36.770
I'll steal you away with love

21:36.770 --> 21:37.690
Don't cry

21:37.690 --> 21:39.900
On your hesitating nape

21:39.900 --> 21:41.770
I'll leave a mark

21:41.770 --> 21:42.440
Don't cry

21:42.440 --> 21:44.540
I can't lie

21:44.540 --> 21:48.530
Nothing can stop me now

21:48.530 --> 21:53.950
I can't move without you

21:53.950 --> 21:56.250
Choose my hand

21:56.250 --> 21:58.460
Your lovely eyes make me feel so dizzy

21:58.460 --> 22:01.130
Can I steal you away tonight

22:01.130 --> 22:05.630
I want to lay bare your sweet heat

22:05.630 --> 22:07.880
My heart is pounding, lovely eyes

22:07.880 --> 22:10.550
You seduce me with your gestures

22:10.550 --> 22:15.200
I have a feeling you'll drive me crazy

22:15.200 --> 22:17.530
I won't let you go

22:17.530 --> 22:19.730
I won't let you have her

22:19.730 --> 22:24.730
My love for you won't stop

24:05.960 --> 24:07.730
I missed you, my lady.

24:07.730 --> 24:09.660
I've been really looking forward to seeing you.

24:09.660 --> 24:10.970
Uta Pri!
